{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3476","id":4520043536,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABDWpkEA","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3476","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3476.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3476.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3476","number":3476,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"cli: distinguish no match from ambiguous match when resolving users","user":{"login":"YpNo","id":883643,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MzY0Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/883643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo","html_url":"https://github.com/YpNo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`headscale users destroy` and `headscale users rename` resolve the target with\r\n`resolveSingleUser`, which treated every result count other than one as\r\n\"multiple users match query, specify an ID\". A name that matches nobody got the\r\nsame message, which points the operator in the wrong direction.\r\n\r\nAn explicit `--identifier 0` had a second problem: the flag default is -1, so 0\r\npassed the \"is a flag set\" check and was sent to the API as `id=0`, which the\r\nlist endpoint treats as \"no filter\". The CLI then received every user and\r\nfailed with the same ambiguous-match error.\r\n\r\nThis change:\r\n\r\n- returns \"no user matches query\" when the list comes back empty\r\n- keeps \"multiple users match query, specify an ID\" for two or more matches\r\n  (OIDC users can share a name, see #3429)\r\n- rejects an explicit zero or negative `--identifier` before calling the API\r\n\r\n`TestResolveSingleUser` now asserts the specific sentinel error for each case\r\ninstead of just \"an error\", and covers the `--identifier 0` regression.\r\n\r\nThe destroy prompt also now says that nodes owned by the user must be deleted\r\nor moved first, since that is the precondition the API enforces and the prompt\r\nonly mentioned pre-auth keys.\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the CONTRIBUTING.md file\r\n- [ ] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [x] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md","created_at":"2026-09-13T17:51:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T18:00:16Z","closed_at":"2026-09-25T18:00:16Z","merged_at":"2026-09-25T18:00:15Z","merge_commit_sha":"3746ad20dbbc75cd2ee85cf4ff58dcc4cd4d549e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n